WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.334
The future of Sudan is in

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.211
the hands of two people.

00:00:03.211 --> 00:00:03.878
The conflict,

00:00:03.878 --> 00:00:04.170
which you're

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.130
probably hearing a lot

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.297
about in the news right now,

00:00:06.297 --> 00:00:08.466
is between the Sudanese Armed Forces

00:00:08.466 --> 00:00:09.676
led by one general

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.302
and the Rapid Support Forces,

00:00:11.302 --> 00:00:13.304
a militia led by another general.

00:00:13.304 --> 00:00:14.597
Both of these guys command

00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:16.349
a lot of power and wealth.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.726
Both are stopping Sudan

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:19.269
from becoming a democracy

00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:21.229
and neither want to give up power.

00:00:21.229 --> 00:00:22.022
And if they don't come

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.314
to an agreement soon,

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:25.567
this could turn into a full on civil war

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:26.484
in Sudan,

00:00:26.484 --> 00:00:28.778
one that might be fueled by outsiders.

00:00:28.778 --> 00:00:30.321
It will be their third civil war

00:00:30.321 --> 00:00:33.158
since they gained independence in 1956.

